@Rich Mole: regarding foreign buyer impacts, the areas most popular for them are pretty much in free fall right now.

http://vancouversun.com/opinion/columnists/douglas-todd-is-china-popping-vancouvers-housing-bubble

The market is just plain WEIRD with the way it is compressing. High end areas generally favored by foreign money are falling and sales activity has declined. Other areas with lower price points - and more likely to be influenced by something like the "BC Home Owner Mortgage and Equity Partnership" program - are seeing increases. It's a strange dynamic.
